From f966f7e7acebbb1250ee8109ad6256ab7281d848 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:22:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] fix(tools): parse DeepSeek DSML tool calls and keep them
 out of the chat
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DeepSeek models wrap native tool-call tags in a DSML token written with
fullwidth bars (<｜DSML｜invoke name="f"><｜DSML｜parameter name="k"
string="true">). When a server does not parse them, or on the tool-limit
final turn where the tools are dropped, they arrived as plain text: the text
parser did not recognise them, so the call never ran and the raw markup was
shown in the chat.

- messageContent: normalizeDsmlToolCalls() reduces DSML tags to plain
  <invoke>/<parameter>; DSML blocks and stray DSML tags join the streaming
  control-token patterns so they are not shown while streaming.
- parseToolCallsFromText normalises DSML first; <invoke>/<parameter> accept
  extra attributes (string="true"); containsToolCallMarkup detects DSML.
- Tool-limit final answer: when the model's reply strips to nothing (markup
  only), show the completed tool results instead of "(No response)".

Ported from fl4p/off-grid-ai-mobile 3c58b8f77 / 3f39fc319 (Fabian), adapted to
the current tool loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
